descriptionByLocale.en:
Ski/Snowboard Monitors

Champittet College, a reference school in the German region since 1903, offers excellent training to generations of Swiss and foreign students. Its unique spirit revolves around academic performance, multilingualism and values such as respect and trust. The College is part of the North Anglia Education family, the world leader in international schools with 88 schools in 32 countries.

In this dynamic environment, both local and international, we are now looking for ski instructors to mentor and accompany our students in our ski camp, which will take place in Fiesch from 15 to 18 March 2027.

Profile sought

• You will be responsible for accompanying a group of ski children during the day and participating in certain activities in the evening (night raquettes, night skiing, statue building, swimming pool, etc.);

• You want to invest fully in the success of this camp;

• You have a very good ski mastery and are comfortable on the slopes;

• You are ideally benefiting from a Youth and Sport (J+S) Ski or Snowboard training;

• You have a good command of English;

• You are 18 or older;

• You are a Swiss national or have a work permit valid in Switzerland;

• You are able to present a blank criminal record.

Accommodation in Fiesch and meals will be taken care of by the Champittet College throughout the stay.

If you are passionate about the field of education and want to join our team, we invite you to submit your application directly online via our website.

